WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.632 --> 00:00:04.233
At last the Caterpillar spoke to Alice.

2
00:00:04.253 --> 00:00:05.173
"Who are you?"

3
00:00:05.193 --> 00:00:07.134
he asked in a sleepy voice.

4
00:00:07.254 --> 00:00:09.035
This was not the best way to start a conversation.

5
00:00:09.055 --> 00:00:14.277
Alice replied rather shyly, "I hardly know, sir.

6
00:00:31.844 --> 00:00:34.225
At least I know who I was when I got up this morning.

7
00:00:34.945 --> 00:00:37.166
But I've changed several times since then."

8
00:00:38.586 --> 00:00:40.606
"What do you mean by that?

9
00:00:41.287 --> 00:00:44.448
Explain yourself," the Caterpillar said.

10
00:00:44.468 --> 00:00:49.909
Alice tried to be polite even though the Caterpillar seemed rather rude.

11
00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:52.990
"I'm afraid I can't put it more clearly, sir.

12
00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.831
Being so many different sizes in one day is confusing."

13
00:00:56.851 --> 00:00:59.592
"No, it isn't."

14
00:01:01.592 --> 00:01:04.773
"Perhaps you haven't had the chance to find that out yet," Alice said.

15
00:01:04.793 --> 00:01:08.774
"When you change into a butterfly, you'll probably feel quite strange."

16
00:01:08.794 --> 00:01:12.755
"I will not," the Caterpillar said.

17
00:01:12.775 --> 00:01:19.657
"You may feel differently than I do," Alice said, still trying to be polite.

18
00:01:19.677 --> 00:01:23.558
"But turning into a butterfly would feel very strange to me."

19
00:01:23.578 --> 00:01:29.000
"You!" The Caterpillar's voice was full of scorn.

20
00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.142
"Who are you?"

21
00:01:33.563 --> 00:01:37.466
And that brought them right back to the beginning of their conversation.

22
00:01:38.547 --> 00:01:41.269
Alice felt annoyed by the Caterpillar's remarks.

23
00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:45.793
She stood as tall as she could and looked straight at him.

24
00:01:45.813 --> 00:01:49.616
"I think you should tell me who you are first."

25
00:01:55.921 --> 00:01:59.744
This was another puzzling question that Alice couldn't answer.

26
00:02:00.896 --> 00:02:04.998
The Caterpillar was in such a bad mood that she wanted to leave.

27
00:02:06.298 --> 00:02:07.699
She started to walk away.

28
00:02:07.719 --> 00:02:10.760
"Come back!"

29
00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.881
the Caterpillar called after her.

30
00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:16.442
"I have something important to say!"

31
00:02:18.923 --> 00:02:24.566
This sounded interesting, so Alice walked back to the mushroom and waited for him to speak.

32
00:02:24.586 --> 00:02:31.205
"Don't lose your temper," the Caterpillar said.

33
00:02:36.728 --> 00:02:37.348
that all?"

34
00:02:38.589 --> 00:02:41.910
Alice couldn't believe how angry he made her feel.

35
00:02:41.931 --> 00:02:50.435
"No." For a few minutes, the Caterpillar sat silently, ignoring Alice.

36
00:02:52.296 --> 00:02:55.638
She was going to leave, but she really had nothing else to do.

37
00:02:57.539 --> 00:02:59.040
So she decided to wait.

38
00:03:00.864 --> 00:03:04.347
Perhaps the Caterpillar would have something interesting to say after all.

39
00:03:06.848 --> 00:03:08.650
Finally he spoke to her again.

40
00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:13.993
"So you think you've changed?"

41
00:03:14.013 --> 00:03:19.357
"Oh, yes," Alice said, happy that he was listening at last.

42
00:03:19.377 --> 00:03:22.379
"First I'm bigger, and then I'm smaller.

43
00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.401
I don't stay the same size for more than a few minutes."

44
00:03:26.362 --> 00:03:28.844
The Caterpillar looked Alice up and down.

45
00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:33.242
"What size do you want to be?"

46
00:03:33.262 --> 00:03:35.824
"I don't really care.

47
00:03:35.844 --> 00:03:38.946
I just don't like changing so often, you know?"

48
00:03:41.068 --> 00:03:44.770
"No, I don't know," the Caterpillar replied.

49
00:03:45.931 --> 00:03:47.132
Alice said nothing.

50
00:03:48.052 --> 00:03:53.056
She'd never met such a disagreeable creature, and she was losing her temper.

51
00:03:54.176 --> 00:03:56.118
The Caterpillar interrupted her thoughts.

52
00:03:56.138 --> 00:03:58.980
"Are you happy now?"

53
00:04:01.108 --> 00:04:05.630
"I'd like to be larger because three inches is such a horrible size."

54
00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:10.312
"Three inches is the perfect height!"

55
00:04:11.152 --> 00:04:17.715
The Caterpillar stretched upright as he spoke, showing that he was exactly three inches high.

56
00:04:17.735 --> 00:04:21.857
"But I'm not used to it!"

57
00:04:22.357 --> 00:04:23.177
Alice moaned.

58
00:04:23.197 --> 00:04:28.840
"You'll get used to it in time," said the Caterpillar.

59
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.723
Alice waited, hoping the Caterpillar would say something more.

60
00:04:36.586 --> 00:04:39.708
Eventually he yawned twice, and shook himself.

61
00:04:44.292 --> 00:04:46.414
Then he got down from the mushroom.

62
00:04:52.719 --> 00:04:58.504
side makes you grow taller," the Caterpillar said, crawling through the grass.

63
00:04:59.708 --> 00:05:03.331
"And the other side makes you smaller."

64
00:05:04.711 --> 00:05:08.034
Alice wondered what in the world he was talking about.

65
00:05:08.054 --> 00:05:10.275
"One side of what?

66
00:05:10.875 --> 00:05:12.496
The other side of what?"

67
00:05:12.937 --> 00:05:13.437
she thought.

68
00:05:13.457 --> 00:05:15.498
"Of the mushroom!"

69
00:05:16.019 --> 00:05:19.941
The Caterpillar replied as if Alice had asked her questions aloud.

70
00:05:21.082 --> 00:05:23.704
And in another moment, he was out of sight.
